<p><strong>Harihara I</strong> and <strong>Bukka I</strong>, sons of <strong>Immadi Pulipati</strong>, founded the Vijayanagara Empire in <span style='color: var(--warning);'>1336 CE</span> after escaping death from the Delhi Sultanate’s forces. They were aided by <strong>Basava Kalyana</strong> and the sage <strong>Vidyaranya</strong>. The empire’s first capital was <strong>Anegondi</strong>, later shifted to <strong>Vijayanagar</strong> (near Hospet in Karnataka).</p>

