    <p>When a question asks “Which climate type supports <em>sal</em> forest?”, recall that <strong>sal (Shorea robusta)</strong> thrives in <strong>Cwa / Cwb</strong> – <em>Humid Subtropical with dry winter</em> (average annual rainfall 1200‑1500 mm, temperature 20‑30°C).</p>

